Skip flash-attn vec when the subgroup is wider than 32.

flash_attn_vec_split.wgsl reduces P*V with subgroupShuffleDown. The first
delta is subgroup_size/2 (32 on a 64-wide subgroup when D_SPLIT is 4), and
the Q*K broadcast shuffles from a lane up to subgroup_size-D_SPLIT. That
pattern is the one GCN (wave64) D3D12 paths have miscompiled. The tile
shader uses scalar subgroupAdd / subgroupMax and does not shuffle across
the 32-lane boundary, so decode stays on WebGPU.

The correctness probe also checks a small f16 matmul and an f16 workgroup
reduction (known answers 10 and 72) and a scalar subgroupAdd of lane ids.
Those failures disable the device. A shuffle-down by 32 is only logged;
vec stays off for every subgroup wider than 32 even if that one shuffle
matches. If the tile shader cannot hold Q_TILE subgroups, the probe
disables WebGPU instead of letting attention return without writing.

A probed size of 32 keeps the vec path, which is the NVIDIA measurement
from 2026-11-09. This is not a claim that a Radeon was retested.

